1
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
The new morning we've finally found

2
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
is being hampered by the past.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

6
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
but the past so full of remorse.

8
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

9
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

10
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

11
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

12
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

13
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
It's about now that a teardrop

14
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

15
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

16
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

17
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Will this rain ever stop?

18
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

19
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
I've been freezing for a long time.

20
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

21
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

22
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

23
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

24
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
Tsutsumarete iikana

25
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Today, the rain falls again;

26
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

27
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

28
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

29
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

30
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

31
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

32
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

33
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The Immortal Legion

34
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The Immortal Legion

35
00:01:55,010 --> 00:01:57,010
It hurts...

36
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,760
Help me...

37
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,760
I'm starving!

38
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,930
Water...!

39
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:03,100
It hurts!

40
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:06,600
"Not yet finished experimenting"?

41
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,390
This in itself is the experiment!

42
00:02:08,390 --> 00:02:09,850
It was a success!

43
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:16,360
The ultimate soldiers that never die, betray, and always fight according to our orders.

44
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:20,110
An immortal army has been created!

45
00:02:21,410 --> 00:02:22,950
Pa...pa?

46
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:25,290
That's right!

47
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:27,830
I am your father!

48
00:02:27,830 --> 00:02:31,210
Now, listen closely to what I'm about to say.

49
00:02:31,210 --> 00:02:36,130
Currently, there are several rebels targeting these headquarters!

50
00:02:36,130 --> 00:02:37,670
Papa!

51
00:02:38,010 --> 00:02:39,340
You all are to-

52
00:03:07,410 --> 00:03:08,660
Ouch...

53
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:10,710
That hurts.

54
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:11,790
That hurts!

55
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:12,420
Pain!

56
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:13,540
That hurts...

57
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:15,250
Ouch...

58
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:16,380
It hurts...

59
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:17,420
The pain...

60
00:03:29,890 --> 00:03:31,980
What a huge gate.

61
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:34,350
I don't like the feeling it gives off.

62
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:36,150
Is this really the place?

63
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:36,940
Yeah.

64
00:03:37,650 --> 00:03:39,400
It looks exactly as Al described it.

65
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:42,650
Who the heck is that?

66
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,280
Number 66.

67
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,910
Barry the Chopper.

68
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:49,740
He was Slicer's partner.

69
00:04:06,970 --> 00:04:10,010
Open...!

70
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:13,690
Dammit...!

71
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:15,730
How the hell are we supposed to open this?!

72
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:19,770
Step aside.

73
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,200
It opened-

74
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:46,300
Order the soldiers from Central that are fighting with the Briggs forces and Mustang to retreat.

75
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:53,430
Oh? Are you going to shoot?

76
00:04:57,650 --> 00:04:59,940
Looks like your men aren't very disciplined.

77
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:06,650
If you don't hurry up and have them retreat,

78
00:05:06,650 --> 00:05:09,570
the soldiers from Briggs will continue to fight with no mercy.

79
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:13,200
Wouldn't it bother you if you lost every single one of your soldiers?

80
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:29,890
Shut the northern, southern, eastern, and western gates that allow entry into the Central Headquarters!

81
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:35,060
Don't let a single enemy force from Briggs or Mustang's party enter!

82
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:40,060
So you're rotten, but it looks like you've still retained a set of testicles.

83
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:42,070
Don't get too cocky, bitch!

84
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:46,240
I'll have all of you monkeys from Briggs crushed-

85
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,040
Huh?

86
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,710
Oh, this one.

87
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:04,590
You're not supposed to interfere.

88
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:09,050
I was told to defeat you.

89
00:06:10,090 --> 00:06:11,890
What a drag...

90
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:15,470
You've just created another spot for me at the top.

91
00:06:15,850 --> 00:06:18,640
I thank you, Homunculus!

92
00:06:18,770 --> 00:06:25,440
You've saved me from having to stain this celebrated sword passed down in my family for generations!

93
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:35,740
You-

94
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:50,550
They won't die?!

95
00:06:52,390 --> 00:06:53,890
It hurts...

96
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,350
I'm starving!

97
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:00,890
It hurts!

98
00:07:00,230 --> 00:07:02,100
The pain!

99
00:07:02,190 --> 00:07:06,150
Brother!

100
00:07:06,150 --> 00:07:07,400
Don't tell me...!

101
00:07:11,110 --> 00:07:13,910
Did they attach souls to dolls?!

102
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:16,200
Dammit! There's no end to them!

103
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,240
What the hell are these things?!

104
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,330
Hell if I know!

105
00:07:19,330 --> 00:07:21,410
Why aren't they dying?!

106
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,420
This is bad.

107
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:25,710
If we were to let them outside...!

108
00:07:32,090 --> 00:07:33,640
Did something happen?

109
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,760
No idea.

110
00:07:34,970 --> 00:07:38,140
I heard Colonel Mustang pulled a coup d'etat.

111
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:40,310
How frightening.

112
00:07:40,310 --> 00:07:42,350
There, there. Don't cry.

113
00:07:46,150 --> 00:07:47,230
What do we do...

114
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:50,780
You-

115
00:07:52,950 --> 00:07:54,780
Oh no! They're getting out!

116
00:08:04,830 --> 00:08:07,750
My bad, I sealed off the exit.

117
00:08:07,750 --> 00:08:09,210
Don't worry about it.

118
00:08:09,210 --> 00:08:12,300
If you hadn't done it, I would have destroyed the exit myself.

119
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,970
Now we can prepare for the worst!

120
00:08:15,090 --> 00:08:19,390
Okay, so now that we don't have to worry about them getting out...

121
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:22,270
...let's show them what we've got!

122
00:08:26,690 --> 00:08:28,190
It hurts!

123
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,570
So much pain!

124
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,780
How dare they make something like this...!

125
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:39,780
Guess we have to go through these guys first to give the old guy a beatdown.

126
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:45,870
This is gonna be rough!

127
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:52,090
Mustang is currently escaping in an ice cream truck!

128
00:08:52,090 --> 00:08:53,590
Barricade the main roads!

129
00:08:54,130 --> 00:08:57,760
The truck may look normal,
but it's filled with weapons and ammo!

130
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:58,970
Don't let your guard down!

131
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:08,770
A-A bear!

132
00:09:08,770 --> 00:09:10,980
A bear with a mohawk!

133
00:09:14,650 --> 00:09:15,780
Signal lost.

134
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:19,030
A bear with a mohawk...?

135
00:09:19,030 --> 00:09:21,330
Captain Buccaneer from the Northern Army.

136
00:09:21,950 --> 00:09:25,250
Colonel, it seems like it'll be difficult to enter the city.

137
00:09:26,790 --> 00:09:28,420
Yeah.

138
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:35,550
An ice cream truck, huh...?

139
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:42,260
I wonder if they're doing well.

140
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:49,350
But it's irritating that I can't fight alongside them.

141
00:09:49,350 --> 00:09:53,070
I never knew how annoying it can be to wait.

142
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:59,950
I've been hearing this sound since yesterday.

143
00:10:00,490 --> 00:10:02,950
Hey Alphonse, what is that sound?

144
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:06,250
Selim's playing with my head.

145
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:16,130
He may be a monster on the inside, but I guess he's still a brat.

146
00:10:25,310 --> 00:10:26,930
Make him stop, Alphonse!

147
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:30,140
Make him stop those noises!

148
00:10:30,140 --> 00:10:31,350
It's morse code!

149
00:10:31,350 --> 00:10:33,190
Signals the army uses for communication!

150
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:42,530
He's telling someone our current location-

151
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:05,300
Hi.

152
00:11:05,930 --> 00:11:09,600
Thanks for coming to pick me up, Kimblee.

153
00:11:11,060 --> 00:11:15,480
Seriously... please stop giving me extra work.

154
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:19,280
Come on, give me a break.

155
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,780
I won't let my guard down again.

156
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:45,010
W-What are these things?!

157
00:11:45,010 --> 00:11:46,800
You tricked me, Envy!

158
00:11:46,970 --> 00:11:49,810
D-Did not!

159
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:51,810
Immortality is just beyond-

160
00:11:51,850 --> 00:11:52,810
Oww!

161
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:55,350
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

162
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:09,120
You bitch!!

163
00:12:27,550 --> 00:12:29,390
Yes!!

164
00:13:11,970 --> 00:13:14,100
Guess who's back?!

165
00:13:25,780 --> 00:13:31,990
Thanks for bringing me here, little brat.

166
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:40,960
Why are there soldiers here?

167
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:42,670
Are they here to make us leave?

168
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,630
Oh no... there's nowhere else to go.

169
00:13:47,510 --> 00:13:49,300
W-What's this all about?

170
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:52,640
Don't tell me they've found out where we're hiding...

171
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:55,100
Oh no, Alphonse!

172
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:56,730
Hang on, Doctor!

173
00:13:57,020 --> 00:14:00,560
What if they found out you're Doctor Marcoh?!

174
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:03,900
But I can't just sit back and watch...

175
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,860
Take a moment to calm down.

176
00:14:07,110 --> 00:14:12,070
If you were to be taken hostage,
it would only hurt Alphonse and the others.

177
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:15,370
It's dangerous to just move around without thinking.

178
00:14:15,370 --> 00:14:16,790
Let's stay put.

179
00:14:16,790 --> 00:14:17,960
Yeah? Yeah?

180
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:34,720
Are you alone?

181
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:37,770
I heard that Gluttony was here with you.

182
00:14:38,230 --> 00:14:41,230
I made use of him.

183
00:14:41,230 --> 00:14:42,690
You ate him?

184
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:44,150
Your own comrade?

185
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:48,570
Not a comrade. We're part of the same being.

186
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:52,030
We were born from the same father.

187
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:55,620
Think of it as "coming back together", per se.

188
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:57,580
I see.

189
00:14:59,330 --> 00:15:00,540
Mr. Heinkel!

190
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:09,130
Wow, you're still alive?

191
00:15:09,590 --> 00:15:13,550
Can't underestimate a chimera's survival power, after all.

192
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:15,970
Mr. Heinkel!

193
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:20,180
Dammit!

194
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:22,810
Let go!

195
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,810
I won't let you get away.

196
00:15:25,110 --> 00:15:26,520
You-

197
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,620
Don't know when to give up, do you.

198
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,300
Stop running away.

199
00:16:06,610 --> 00:16:07,860
What?

200
00:16:09,530 --> 00:16:10,860
I knew it wouldn't work.

201
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,360
That's as far as you're going to get,
Major General Armstrong!

202
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:19,870
A shoot-on-sight order has been issued for your treason!

203
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,160
Ready!

204
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:25,210
Fire!

205
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:28,210
Idiot.

206
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:31,210
Placing your men in this situation is just foolish.

207
00:16:47,230 --> 00:16:49,940
Here's to hoping that did some damage to you...

208
00:16:52,530 --> 00:16:54,780
I've got you now.

209
00:16:57,200 --> 00:17:00,740
Didn't get the wrong one this time.

210
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:06,710
Female general...

211
00:17:07,170 --> 00:17:08,420
...must die.

212
00:17:19,550 --> 00:17:22,520
Sister!!

213
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:26,060
Are you all right?!

214
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:31,820
Who are you even talking to, Alex?!

215
00:17:32,190 --> 00:17:34,740
Glad to see you're safe.

216
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:38,160
And so, what is that thing?

217
00:17:38,910 --> 00:17:40,490
A Homunculus.

218
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:42,870
A bullet isn't enough to even move him an inch.

219
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:46,410
Maybe a little budge with a cannon.

220
00:17:46,410 --> 00:17:47,670
Oh, my!

221
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:51,790
This is my specialty!

222
00:17:53,050 --> 00:17:58,430
Please let your brother, Alex, handle this!

223
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:01,300
Come, monster!

224
00:18:03,510 --> 00:18:06,680
Such a drag...

225
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:17,530
Don't mind me...

226
00:18:18,990 --> 00:18:21,280
Hurry up... and escape...

227
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:22,370
No!

228
00:18:22,370 --> 00:18:24,200
Don't be stupid.

229
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,540
At this rate, neither of us will make it.

230
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:31,960
If you leave me behind, at least you may be able to survive.

231
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:33,670
I said, no!

232
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:38,420
Focus on living for now!

233
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:39,720
Idiot!

234
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:42,180
Take a good look at reality.

235
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:45,140
We're put against Kimblee and Pride.

236
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:51,020
Just leave me behind...!

237
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:53,900
Don't give up!

238
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,860
I'll save you for sure!

239
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:01,950
Dammit...!

240
00:19:01,950 --> 00:19:04,700
Move, stupid leg!

241
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:11,250
We can't lose here!

242
00:19:13,330 --> 00:19:15,500
Mr. Heinkel, hang onto me!

243
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:17,590
Don't you dare give up!

244
00:19:17,590 --> 00:19:20,670
You siblings are so...

245
00:19:22,010 --> 00:19:27,680
Why do you try to save others
when you're all damaged as well?

246
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,270
I made a promise.

247
00:19:33,230 --> 00:19:35,110
I made a promise with Brother,

248
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:39,400
that we won't let anyone die again.

249
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:47,660
You're right.

250
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:52,290
I recall even Kimblee saying that "if you survive, you win."

251
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:58,170
Thanks to that, I remembered that I had something good with me.

252
00:20:04,010 --> 00:20:06,180
Why do you have this?

253
00:20:06,930 --> 00:20:11,930
I picked it up at the mines to the north after being abandoned by Kimblee...

254
00:20:13,060 --> 00:20:14,560
A philosopher's stone...

255
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:18,270
We really may be able to beat them if we have this.

256
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:19,820
But still!

257
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:21,860
Yeah, I know.

258
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:24,990
This is made of human lives, right?

259
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:33,040
I've heard from your brother that you guys don't want to use this to return to your bodies.

260
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:35,000
In that case...

261
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:41,550
In that case, use them to save the world; not for yourselves.

262
00:20:43,090 --> 00:20:45,510
I'm asking you because you're willing to acknowledge them as human lives,

263
00:20:45,630 --> 00:20:49,510
even after being reduced to such a state.

264
00:20:50,510 --> 00:20:52,980
I can understand their feelings.

265
00:20:54,940 --> 00:21:01,020
No matter what they may look like now, they still want to fight to protect what's precious to them.

266
00:21:02,110 --> 00:21:05,450
Give them a chance to fight too.

267
00:21:12,450 --> 00:21:13,620
Okay.

268
00:21:14,870 --> 00:21:16,620
Give them a good beatdown,

269
00:21:18,130 --> 00:21:19,590
Alphonse.

270
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:20,840
Yeah.

271
00:21:23,260 --> 00:21:25,720
Let's fight them together.

272
00:21:28,590 --> 00:21:31,310
This cloud of dust is annoying.

273
00:21:31,310 --> 00:21:34,220
Should I blow it away with an explosion?

274
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:35,100
No,

275
00:21:35,390 --> 00:21:38,980
they're both still inside it.

276
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:40,980
Besides, he won't be able to escape without his legs-

277
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:02,380
Oh, my.

278
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:04,050
Instead of escaping, you...

279
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:14,770
Marvelous.

280
00:22:16,890 --> 00:22:21,980
Very entertaining, Alphonse Elric!

281
00:22:28,950 --> 00:22:32,500
Ever since that day passed,

282
00:22:28,950 --> 00:22:32,500
Ano hi kara zutto

283
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:36,750
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

284
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:36,750
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

285
00:22:37,290 --> 00:22:42,300
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

286
00:22:37,290 --> 00:22:42,300
Itami wo kasanetemo

287
00:22:42,300 --> 00:22:47,410
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

288
00:22:42,300 --> 00:22:47,410
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

289
00:22:48,890 --> 00:22:50,850
I'll never be able

290
00:22:48,890 --> 00:22:50,850
Mou modorenai

291
00:22:50,850 --> 00:22:53,350
to return to those days.

292
00:22:50,850 --> 00:22:53,350
Ikutsumo no hibi

293
00:22:53,350 --> 00:22:58,440
I'm still powerless.

294
00:22:53,350 --> 00:22:58,440
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

295
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:03,690
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

296
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:03,690
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

297
00:23:03,690 --> 00:23:09,560
memories of when you were still with me.

298
00:23:03,690 --> 00:23:09,560
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

299
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:12,580
I long to become

300
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:12,580
Kyou yori motto

301
00:23:12,580 --> 00:23:15,330
stronger than I am now,

302
00:23:12,580 --> 00:23:15,330
Tsuyoku naritai

303
00:23:15,330 --> 00:23:20,470
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

304
00:23:15,330 --> 00:23:20,470
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

305
00:23:20,470 --> 00:23:22,840
If the wind happens to stop

306
00:23:20,470 --> 00:23:22,840
Arukitsuzukete

307
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:25,550
in the midst of my long journey,

308
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:25,550
Kaze ga yandara

309
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:30,260
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

310
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:30,260
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

311
00:23:31,010 --> 00:23:37,600
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

312
00:23:31,010 --> 00:23:37,600
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

313
00:23:38,770 --> 00:23:43,150
A rainbow spans across the sky.

314
00:23:38,770 --> 00:23:43,150
Niji ga kakaruyo

315
00:23:59,870 --> 00:24:05,540
If it's a fight between man and man, choose the path you believe is right.

316
00:24:06,210 --> 00:24:11,840
Only a fool would stand indecisive after being frightened at the thought of being soiled by the mud.

317
00:24:13,300 --> 00:24:17,300
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

318
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:21,830
Episode 52, Combined Strength.

319
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:21,830
Combined Strength

320
00:24:22,620 --> 00:24:26,170
It is beyond the point of hesitation.
